WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:06.580
In two days, on the day of my seventeenth birthday,

00:06.580 --> 00:08.910
I, Nana Nanase, will marry Tomoya Chiba!

00:10.870 --> 00:12.040
What?!

00:12.040 --> 00:13.910
Hold on, Nana! What are you saying?!

00:13.910 --> 00:16.160
Marriage is forever, you know.
You should think a little harder about it...

00:16.410 --> 00:18.120
That's not the problem she should be worried about.

00:18.120 --> 00:22.040
Nana, this isn't the world we belong in.

00:22.040 --> 00:23.250
What?

00:23.500 --> 00:25.950
She means we're in a parallel antenna!

00:25.950 --> 00:27.080
Parallel world.

00:27.080 --> 00:28.080
Yeah, that!

00:28.080 --> 00:29.540
So basically...

00:29.540 --> 00:31.700
Oh, is that it?

00:32.200 --> 00:36.410
Here I was thinking it was some world where
the butterfly effect had changed a ton of things.

00:36.410 --> 00:37.830
Man, I was so close.

00:38.250 --> 00:41.330
Nana is making absolutely no sense to me right now.

00:41.790 --> 00:46.200
So you guys are from my world, which isn't this world.

00:46.200 --> 00:48.120
Okay, I got it, yeah.

00:48.120 --> 00:50.160
Well, good.

00:50.160 --> 00:55.830
If we do the Ritual of 4.44 tomorrow,
we can go back to our original world!

00:55.830 --> 00:57.950
I'm not going back.

00:58.160 --> 00:58.950
What?

00:58.950 --> 01:01.250
If I go back to our world,

01:01.250 --> 01:03.580
I'm just gonna be some stupid high school girl.

01:03.580 --> 01:07.370
Compared to that world, this world is much more fun.
I'm gonna be married to a celebrity!

01:07.370 --> 01:08.750
You can't do that!

01:08.750 --> 01:11.080
All of us club members have to go back together!

01:11.080 --> 01:13.330
I'm not in the Radio Research Society.

01:13.330 --> 01:15.540
I don't give a crap about radios!

01:15.540 --> 01:18.660
I just hang out with you guys because it's kind of fun.

01:21.410 --> 01:22.700
I'm back.

01:25.160 --> 01:28.660
If Nana won't go back with us... what do we do?

01:29.080 --> 01:33.120
The Nana in your world will go missing.

01:35.330 --> 01:36.450
She'll be gone.

03:10.470 --> 03:14.620
Before the Wedding Bells Ring

03:15.120 --> 03:17.790
Maybe I shouldn't have said all that stuff...

03:19.410 --> 03:22.200
Nana-chan! Are you awake?

03:23.160 --> 03:24.450
Yeah.

03:26.290 --> 03:28.040
My marriage registration form...?

03:28.040 --> 03:32.750
Yes. I think it'll feel more real
for you if you fill it out yourself.

03:33.080 --> 03:35.160
Tomoya-san's already filled out his part.

03:35.160 --> 03:36.500
Okay.

03:37.000 --> 03:40.330
Hey mom, Tomoya-san's name is wrong.

03:40.330 --> 03:42.750
My, I thought you were the one
who told me he had a different name!

03:42.750 --> 03:44.790
Chiba Tomoya's just his stage name, right?

03:46.160 --> 03:47.870
So that's his real name...

03:48.250 --> 03:50.080
Huh? No way!

03:52.660 --> 03:54.200
Morning light...

03:54.200 --> 03:58.000
We survived the long, cold night...

03:58.000 --> 04:00.950
We survived!

04:00.950 --> 04:03.250
You're making way too big of a deal out of this.

04:03.250 --> 04:05.540
I suppose it was a little bit cold...

04:05.540 --> 04:07.910
Has anyone seen the other Asuka?

04:07.910 --> 04:10.000
You're right, she's not here...

04:10.000 --> 04:12.250
She was with us when we fell asleep, though.

04:12.250 --> 04:15.790
As always, she up and disappears
whenever she wants. That silly Seriouska...

04:15.790 --> 04:17.950
Maybe because you call her Seriouska.

04:18.410 --> 04:20.950
Anyway, shouldn't we be more concerned about Nana?

04:20.950 --> 04:22.040
Yeah...

04:22.450 --> 04:27.290
Who would've guessed Nana would choose marrying
a celebrity over coming home with us?

04:27.290 --> 04:30.500
Given her personality, anyone would've guessed that.

04:30.500 --> 04:33.500
Um, I've been wondering about this for a while,

04:33.500 --> 04:37.580
but why does Nana-senpai hang out
with the Radio Research Society?

04:37.580 --> 04:44.950
Well, last spring, when we'd all just started high school,
I borrowed a crystal radio from Chloe.

04:45.790 --> 04:48.500
I figured we could use it to attract people to our club.

04:49.500 --> 04:52.160
And Nana walked up and started staring at it.

04:52.540 --> 04:55.540
I asked her if she was into crystal radios, and she said...

04:56.540 --> 04:57.750
Not really.

04:57.940 --> 05:02.160
Come!!
Join the Radio
Research Club!

04:58.080 --> 05:00.200
I just wanted to know what this weird, freaky thing was.

05:02.290 --> 05:07.200
That was all she said that day, but the next day,
I ran into her in the bike parking lot and said hi...

05:07.580 --> 05:09.330
And that's how you became friends?!

05:09.330 --> 05:10.620
No, she totally ignored me.

05:10.620 --> 05:15.000
She ignored me every single day after that,
but I kept trying to talk to her.

05:15.000 --> 05:19.370
After about two months, Nana gave in,
and now she hangs with us.

05:19.370 --> 05:21.950
Wow, Asuka-senpai, you sure are patient...

05:21.950 --> 05:27.790
To be honest, if you'd told me back then that I'd be
friends with Nana, I would've said you were crazy.

05:31.370 --> 05:32.700
Is that...

05:33.200 --> 05:34.540
Nana-senpai...?

05:35.040 --> 05:39.250
I'm not gonna do it! I can't marry him, I just can't!

05:39.250 --> 05:41.080
I'll never, ever marry that guy!

05:41.080 --> 05:44.870
C-calm down, Nana! What in the world happened?!

05:44.870 --> 05:47.660
His name... Tomoya Chiba's real name!

05:47.640 --> 05:49.870
Tomoya Chiyokoba
It's Tomoya Chiyokoba!

05:51.200 --> 05:53.450
Put his last name before my first name, like on the form.

05:53.450 --> 05:55.200
Chiyokoba, Nana?

05:55.750 --> 05:56.700
Chocolate Banana!

05:57.330 --> 05:58.540
Chocolate Banana!

05:58.660 --> 06:00.750
Noooooo!

06:01.000 --> 06:02.120
I get it.

06:02.120 --> 06:03.950
That's a little...

06:03.940 --> 06:05.200
It's awful...

06:04.950 --> 06:07.410
Aww, what's wrong with chocolate bananas?
They're so yummy!

06:07.410 --> 06:08.500
I won't do it!

06:08.500 --> 06:13.330
When my mom remarried, and my legal name
changed to Nana Nanase, four "na"s,

06:13.330 --> 06:17.000
I swore to never marry someone
if they'd make my name even weirder!

06:17.000 --> 06:18.950
I swore I'd never do it!

06:18.950 --> 06:21.250
It's okay, Nana. There, there.

06:27.450 --> 06:29.700
My name is Yaji.
I'm from the Marriage Enforcement Agency!

06:29.700 --> 06:31.540
I'm his colleague, Kitta.

06:31.540 --> 06:32.870
Seriously...?

06:32.870 --> 06:35.750
So they're not teachers in this world, huh...

06:35.750 --> 06:38.290
What's the Marriage Enforcement Agency?

06:38.450 --> 06:42.660
The MEA exists to ensure the smooth realization
of predetermined marriages.

06:42.660 --> 06:47.000
We received a report that an individual had decided
not to marry and was causing trouble.

06:47.000 --> 06:49.450
It looks like you're the girl from that report.

06:49.440 --> 06:51.440
Nana Nanase

06:49.870 --> 06:54.200
Nana Nanase, tomorrow is your seventeenth birthday.

06:54.200 --> 06:57.200
Acting like this the day before your wedding?
How disgraceful!

06:57.200 --> 06:58.500
You need counseling! Come with us!

06:58.500 --> 06:59.290
No!

06:59.290 --> 07:00.830
Hey, let her go!

07:00.830 --> 07:01.750
What are you girls doing?

07:01.750 --> 07:03.700
Y-you shouldn't use force!

07:03.700 --> 07:05.160
My, this is a problem.

07:09.370 --> 07:11.040
They had all these guys?!

07:11.250 --> 07:12.830
You rat bastards...
Bande d'enfoirée...

07:15.040 --> 07:16.000
Oww!

07:17.330 --> 07:19.370
Let go of me, let go, dammit!

07:21.330 --> 07:22.950
Nana!

07:23.370 --> 07:24.910
Oh no, what now?!

07:28.660 --> 07:30.080
More Noizies...

07:30.790 --> 07:32.540
They sure love to give me a hard time...

07:43.660 --> 07:45.790
Did I get all of the ones in this area?

07:45.790 --> 07:47.450
What was that just now?

07:49.250 --> 07:54.250
It seemed like you were looking for something around
here yesterday, so we came to find you.

07:54.250 --> 07:57.000
You were looking for those weird snow bunnies, then?

07:59.330 --> 08:01.790
I call them Noizies.

08:02.660 --> 08:05.500
They're not what I'm looking for, however.

08:06.250 --> 08:08.120
The thing I'm after is much worse.

08:08.750 --> 08:10.080
It's called a Clutter.

08:13.910 --> 08:17.000
Why was I getting all excited about this in the first place...

08:17.450 --> 08:19.700
It's not like I wanted to get married or anything...

08:21.620 --> 08:22.790
Tomoya-san!

08:23.080 --> 08:26.410
Nana-chan! Is it true that you don't want to get married?

08:26.700 --> 08:27.580
Why not?

08:27.580 --> 08:30.620
U-umm, well, you see...

08:31.160 --> 08:32.830
Is it your dad again?

08:32.830 --> 08:33.870
Huh?

08:34.540 --> 08:38.250
He still doesn't want you to marry me. That's it, right?

08:38.250 --> 08:41.000
He's not even your real dad...

08:41.000 --> 08:44.250
N-no, that's not it, I just-

08:44.250 --> 08:48.450
It doesn't matter. It's too late now.

08:48.450 --> 08:50.250
What does that mean?

08:50.620 --> 08:53.120
Nobody's going to let the blushing bride

08:53.120 --> 08:57.040
of megastar Tomoya Chiba get away
from him before her wedding day.

08:58.040 --> 08:59.120
Got it?

09:01.580 --> 09:05.660
As I explained yesterday,
Fragments continue to come into existence.

09:06.080 --> 09:08.700
They are also continuously destroyed.

09:09.330 --> 09:14.200
It starts with those little tears in reality,
like the one you just saw.

09:14.580 --> 09:20.120
After that, those being called Clutters begin
to violently consume and erode at the Fragment.

09:20.750 --> 09:27.200
So basically, you go to these Fragments to kill Clutters
and stop them from destroying those worlds?

09:27.200 --> 09:28.950
That's probably not the case.

09:29.330 --> 09:33.290
Asuka isn't the kind of person to work
that hard for someone that isn't herself.

09:33.290 --> 09:35.410
Wow, that's mean. I'm not saying you're wrong, though.

09:35.410 --> 09:37.540
There's another reason, isn't there?

09:39.580 --> 09:44.700
The world I hail from has experienced a great
amount of erosion and is on the brink of destruction.

09:42.250 --> 09:45.040
Café Octave

09:44.950 --> 09:45.910
Huh?

09:45.910 --> 09:47.620
But we still have a chance.

09:47.950 --> 09:52.250
I can stop our world from being completely
destroyed by killing just one being.

09:52.750 --> 09:54.830
They're called the King of Twilight.

09:55.290 --> 09:56.910
The King of Twilight...?

09:56.910 --> 09:58.290
Who are they?

09:58.660 --> 10:00.450
I'm not sure.

10:00.750 --> 10:06.410
All I know is that they're incredibly powerful,
and they grant some of that power to Clutters.

10:07.660 --> 10:13.450
By looking for Clutters, I might be able
to find a way to get to the King of Twilight,

10:15.120 --> 10:17.700
and I can save my world.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.910
Got it. Thank you for telling us all that.

10:24.450 --> 10:26.750
Forget about the Clutter for now.

10:27.080 --> 10:31.870
First, we have to get Nana back,
and return you to your original world.

10:34.000 --> 10:35.830
This isn't good! Asuka, hide!

10:35.830 --> 10:36.410
Huh?

10:36.410 --> 10:37.450
Wait, which one of us?

10:37.450 --> 10:39.160
Both of you! Come on!

10:42.500 --> 10:47.040
My, everyone, I can't believe you came
for tea without inviting me!

10:47.040 --> 10:49.750
Y-Yes, and we are terribly sorry about it!

10:50.500 --> 10:55.580
I'm merely joking. Have you heard
the news about Nana-san?

10:55.580 --> 10:57.000
Huh? What news...?

10:57.000 --> 11:00.750
Her ceremony has been expedited and
is going to happen right now!

11:00.750 --> 11:03.200
Let's hurry ourselves over to the MEA's chapel...

11:03.200 --> 11:04.750
What?! Why?!

11:05.910 --> 11:07.410
Asuka-senpai!

11:09.540 --> 11:11.200
No choice now. Run!

11:11.200 --> 11:12.700
Whaaaaaaat?!

11:13.080 --> 11:14.370
Grab our bill for us, me!

11:17.200 --> 11:19.580
It is just as Lord Chikuwa told me...

11:19.910 --> 11:23.370
Today, I'd meet a new version of myself!

11:24.040 --> 11:27.040
What do we do? At this rate,
Nana-senpai's going to be married off...

11:27.040 --> 11:29.790
There's only one thing to do: stop it!

11:33.080 --> 11:35.250
Oh my god, I look so cute!

11:40.950 --> 11:43.080
I'm getting swept up in all this again...

11:44.580 --> 11:45.200
Yeah?

11:46.870 --> 11:49.700
How are you doing, Nana-chan? Feeling alright?

11:50.290 --> 11:54.000
He still doesn't want you to marry me. That's it, right?

11:54.700 --> 11:58.830
Umm... I heard you didn't want me to marry him...

12:04.000 --> 12:06.040
I wanted to give this to you.

12:06.700 --> 12:08.950
It's something that used to be yours.

12:10.200 --> 12:15.700
Three years ago, I found it in the trash,
the day after I came to live with you.

12:16.620 --> 12:19.500
You probably wanted to forget about this back then...

12:20.040 --> 12:22.160
But I thought you might want it now.

12:29.250 --> 12:32.500
I'm sorry, Nana-chan. I wish I could protect you...

12:32.500 --> 12:35.160
Just like your real Dad wanted to...

12:35.330 --> 12:36.250
Huh?

12:49.200 --> 12:51.750
Hey Dad, what're you making?

12:52.450 --> 12:55.700
This? It's called a crystal radio.

12:56.160 --> 12:57.410
Want to give it a listen?

12:58.120 --> 13:01.790
I can hear something! How? There aren't any batteries...

13:01.790 --> 13:03.330
Amazing, isn't it?

13:03.330 --> 13:11.580
The crystal in the radio demodulates
the signal from the radio waves.

13:14.080 --> 13:17.950
It might be a little hard for you to understand.
Try to think of it this way.

13:18.540 --> 13:21.500
Crystals have a plus and minus side,
a light and a dark side.

13:22.040 --> 13:26.290
Everything between those sides sticks to one solid belief.

13:26.660 --> 13:29.750
That's how you can hear something
you weren't able to hear before.

13:30.330 --> 13:34.120
I hope you'll be just like that crystal one day, Nana.

13:34.120 --> 13:39.160
I want you to live life according to your principles,
not get swept up in someone else's.

13:39.500 --> 13:42.660
Make it crystal clear what you stand for. Get it?

13:49.750 --> 13:51.160
Don't get swept up...

13:51.580 --> 13:53.370
Make it crystal clear...

13:55.660 --> 13:56.790
It's time.

13:58.750 --> 14:00.330
Here she comes!

14:00.750 --> 14:04.290
This is the young woman who
has stolen Tomoya Chiba's heart!

14:04.290 --> 14:06.580
My, doesn't she look elated!

14:11.910 --> 14:13.200
Let us in!

14:13.660 --> 14:15.290
Tomoya!

14:16.040 --> 14:18.830
Let us in, please!

14:16.500 --> 14:17.830
Tomoya
LOVE

14:22.120 --> 14:23.290
This noise...

14:23.290 --> 14:24.700
How are we gonna get in?

14:24.700 --> 14:28.200
That's obvious! We'll push our way through!

14:28.540 --> 14:30.580
Out of the way!

14:37.000 --> 14:38.700
You look beautiful, Nana.

14:44.040 --> 14:47.410
Only invited attendees and media outlets may enter!

14:47.410 --> 14:49.250
Get back!

14:49.250 --> 14:51.290
Sorry!

14:49.580 --> 14:51.580
Coming through!

14:51.290 --> 14:52.200
I'm really sorry!

14:54.250 --> 14:59.040
Tomoya Chiyokoba, do you take Nana Nanase
as your lawfully wedded wife...

15:00.870 --> 15:01.950
Hey, you!

15:01.950 --> 15:10.910
For better and for worse, in sickness and in health,
as long as you both shall live?

15:11.200 --> 15:12.290
I do.

15:16.370 --> 15:17.120
It's close...

15:17.120 --> 15:18.450
The Clutter's here!

15:20.580 --> 15:25.450
Nanase Nana, do you take Tomoya Chiyokoba
as your lawfully wedded husband,

15:25.830 --> 15:33.620
for better and for worse, in sickness and in health,
as long as you both shall live?

15:35.290 --> 15:36.580
Nana?

15:37.950 --> 15:38.950
I...

15:41.750 --> 15:43.000
I don't!

15:46.290 --> 15:47.370
Nana!

15:51.410 --> 15:52.790
Asuka!

15:59.580 --> 16:01.910
Is that you, Asuka-senpai?

16:02.410 --> 16:05.290
Yes, it's my new self!

16:05.290 --> 16:06.040
What...?

16:08.040 --> 16:09.540
Let's go, Nana!

16:09.540 --> 16:10.450
Yeah!

16:14.540 --> 16:18.370
This won't do... Not in the middle of our ceremony.

16:19.290 --> 16:21.040
I told you, didn't I, Nana?

16:21.750 --> 16:26.540
We were going to make everyone experience
the feelings we had here today...

16:27.160 --> 16:31.250
We were going to make the world feel the same joy!

16:31.250 --> 16:33.910
No! I won't get swept up in everyone else's crap!

16:33.910 --> 16:35.700
I'm going to live my own life!

16:36.120 --> 16:39.580
I'm going to make that fact crystal clear,
just like my dad told me to do!

16:42.580 --> 16:44.750
Come forth, my twilight self!

16:48.750 --> 16:50.120
Duplicate!

17:05.120 --> 17:06.700
Wait, is that...

17:10.540 --> 17:12.250
Nice dodge, Clutter.

17:12.700 --> 17:15.660
No, that hurt quite a bit.

17:17.200 --> 17:22.080
Enough to make me really want to kill you!

17:23.160 --> 17:24.290
Watch out!

17:24.290 --> 17:25.040
Wh-what?!

17:27.500 --> 17:28.330
Asuka!

17:28.330 --> 17:29.660
Nana-senpai!

18:13.870 --> 18:14.660
What?!

18:24.580 --> 18:25.580
Are you okay?!

18:36.750 --> 18:37.370
Um...

18:37.950 --> 18:40.040
Come forth, my twilight self!

18:40.950 --> 18:43.200
Duplicate!

18:47.080 --> 18:48.160
Nana-senpai?!

19:00.410 --> 19:01.500
You creep...

19:02.450 --> 19:04.500
You stupid, no good, creepy bastard!

19:05.500 --> 19:08.580
You seriously thought
I was gonna marry you? Are you crazy?!

19:08.790 --> 19:11.200
And what kind of last name is that?

19:11.200 --> 19:13.080
Chiyokoba? That's frickin' weird!

19:13.080 --> 19:16.250
I am never going to be named "Chocolate Banana"!

19:22.450 --> 19:24.200
You moron!

19:31.200 --> 19:32.000
Nana!

19:40.410 --> 19:45.040
You stupid, sexy bastard!

20:03.250 --> 20:04.290
Thanks.

20:05.660 --> 20:08.750
I never would've imagined
that you'd get to Equalizing level.

20:09.290 --> 20:10.540
Equalizing?

20:11.160 --> 20:16.370
When you overcome your shortcomings and
come close to realizing a complete idea,

20:16.830 --> 20:21.250
you gain the right to become an Equalizer
who can destroy aberrant beings.

20:21.580 --> 20:23.370
Just like you did just now.

20:25.120 --> 20:26.330
Did that make sense to you?

20:27.120 --> 20:31.750
Not really sure, but it sounds like
you can transform now or something?

20:31.750 --> 20:33.580
That's a blunt way of putting it.

20:40.620 --> 20:44.700
Tell me about the King of Twilight. Where are they?

20:45.120 --> 20:46.660
Our king?

20:49.120 --> 20:52.870
How ignorant you are, little one...

20:52.870 --> 20:53.830
What?

20:54.290 --> 20:56.040
One day, you will know...

20:56.540 --> 21:00.580
When you are swallowed by the Twilight...

21:10.080 --> 21:11.500
You okay, Dad?

21:11.500 --> 21:13.330
Y-yes...

21:13.330 --> 21:16.370
Nana-chan, was what happened
just now some kind of surprise?

21:16.370 --> 21:21.450
Hey, so I'm not really the Nana from this world.
I've got to get back to mine.

21:21.450 --> 21:22.250
Huh?

21:24.200 --> 21:29.120
When the real me comes back,
give her that crystal radio.

21:29.500 --> 21:31.290
I left it in that prep room.

21:32.870 --> 21:34.830
Alright, Nana-chan.

21:36.750 --> 21:40.870
A-also, it's kinda creepy when
you use "-chan" after my name.

21:42.870 --> 21:43.870
What...?

21:48.500 --> 21:50.250
I feel kind of bad for me...

21:50.250 --> 21:51.660
Wait, why?

21:51.660 --> 21:56.500
'Cause once I go back to my world,
the me in this world is gonna wake up, right?

21:56.910 --> 21:59.750
And she's gonna realize her wedding has gone
to crap while she wasn't here.

22:00.200 --> 22:06.000
But because we defeated that Clutter,
this world has escaped being consumed by the Twilight.

22:06.200 --> 22:08.160
We've got to be happy with that.

22:09.080 --> 22:12.200
I still don't really get it, but sure, let's go with that.

22:12.200 --> 22:15.540
I can't help but sympathize with myself here, too.

22:15.750 --> 22:18.660
She did say she didn't feel up to getting married.

22:19.120 --> 22:24.200
I'm already married, but I wonder
if I'm actually happy in that life...

22:25.540 --> 22:31.500
I bet Chloe, Yu, Asuka, and Mia are all gonna be okay.

22:32.160 --> 22:39.250
All the girls in this world are working their hardest
to live the lives they want to live.

22:43.500 --> 22:46.330
It's almost 4:44.

22:46.790 --> 22:47.750
Right.

22:51.120 --> 22:55.580
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight!

22:59.540 --> 23:03.540
This is Annie Maxda with
the Twilight Jukebox, signing off.

23:03.790 --> 23:06.870
It's time for me to go once again.

23:08.040 --> 23:10.830
Yeah, that's it. It works great.

23:10.830 --> 23:13.790
It feels like we're a real Radio Research Society!

23:13.790 --> 23:15.500
This was your dad's?

23:15.500 --> 23:19.500
Yeah. My new dad saved it for me.

23:20.040 --> 23:22.750
He freaked out when I asked for it,
like, "How did you know?!"

23:22.750 --> 23:25.950
Wait, did you just call him your 'new dad'?

23:25.950 --> 23:27.540
Did I?

23:27.540 --> 23:29.290
She totally did, right?

23:29.290 --> 23:33.200
Who cares about that? This is way more important.

23:34.200 --> 23:35.000
Here.

23:36.440 --> 23:41.000
Club Application
I would like to join the Radio Research Club.
Nana Nanase
